UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52135880677843
DTSTART:20260604T120000Z
DTEND:20260605T040000Z
DESCRIPTION:NC Trail Days returns to the towns of Elkin and Jonesville\, No
 rth Carolina on the first weekend of June. This four day event celebrates 
 the 'Great Trails State' along with the abundant opportunities for outdoor
  recreation in this part of the Blue Ridge foothills. The event features a
 n array of guided hikes\, several of which are along the NC Mountains-to-S
 ea Trail and the Overmountain Victory National Historic Trail\, as well as
  multiple paddle trips on the Yadkin River. Many of the hikes are themed a
 nd focus on unique regional history such as the popular hidden moonshine s
 tills hike\, or the naturalist hiking series which offers glimpses of the 
 area's ecology and milltown history. In addition to guided and self-guided
  hikes\, the festival offers rock climbing at nearby Stone Mountain and Pi
 lot Mountain State Parks\, cycling\, trail races\, outdoor gear vendors\, 
 live music and more. Nearly all the events are free to attend but may requ
 ire registration. These details will be released with the schedule in Spri
 ng of 2026. Check out www.nctraildays.com for more info until then\, and w
 e hope to see you there!
