DESCRIPTION:Iredell County will host a community Flag Day Ceremony on Frida
 y\, June 12 at 10 a.m. at the Government Center South in Mooresville. The 
 event will bring together county leaders\, veterans\, public safety repres
 entatives\, and local partners to honor the history and symbolism of the A
 merican flag.\n\nThe ceremony will include welcoming remarks\, a presentat
 ion of colors by the Iredell County Sheriff’s Office Honor Guard\, the r
 aising of a Capitol‑flown flag\, a reading reflecting on the significanc
 e of the flag\, and closing recognitions.\n\nCounty Library Director and C
 hair of Iredell County America 250 Juli Moore said the ceremony is an impo
 rtant moment of unity for the community.\n\n“Flag Day reminds us that ou
 r shared history and values are worth honoring together\,” Moore said. 
 “We’re grateful to the veterans\, public safety teams\, and community 
 partners who help keep those values alive.”\n\nThe event is part of Ired
 ell County’s ongoing America 250 efforts\, recognizing the nation’s up
 coming semiquincentennial and highlighting local contributions to American
  history.\n\nCommunity members are invited to attend and join in this brie
 f but meaningful observance.
GEO:35.579866;-80.803643
LOCATION:Government Center South
SUMMARY:Flag Day Ceremony
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/flag-day-ceremony
END:VEVENT
