DESCRIPTION:Dads and grandpas come out and enjoy an early hike solo or with
  the family to get a head start on celbrating Father's Day. This ranger le
 d hike will be on the Pilot Knob Trail and good views and sage dad advice 
 will be abundent. This trail is 0.8 miles and graded moderate so please br
 ing water\, sun protection\, and good hiking shoes. After the hike we invi
 te everyone to stick around for our first annual Dad Olympics! Who can unt
 angle a garden hose fastest? Find the right size socket rench first? Tell 
 the best dad joke? It could be you! Come out and compete with other local 
 dads and grandpas to see who has what it takes to bring home the Best Dad 
 prize!\n\nAll events will take place on the mountain - park in the upper p
 arking lot and look for park staff on the overlooks. This event is weather
  dependent and will be canceled in the event of bad weather. Please RSVP f
 or up to date information - and let us know if you are interested in just 
 the hike\, Dad Olympics\, or both! \n\nRSVP at: pilot.mountain@ncparks.gov
GEO:36.342384;-80.463541
LOCATION:Pilot Mountain State Park\, Mountain Parking Lot on Overlooks. 
