 ty as we come together to honor freedom\, culture\, community\, and the ri
 ch history of Juneteenth through music\, art\, food\, and fellowship. This
  exciting two-day celebration will feature live entertainment\, African dr
 umming\, storytelling\, spoken word\, local artistry\, food vendors\, fami
 ly activities\, bounce houses\, open gym\, community engagement\, and so m
 uch more.\n\nOn Thursday\, June 19\, celebrate with us at the West Souther
 n Pines Center located at 1250 West New York Avenue\, Southern Pines\, NC 
 from 4 PM to 9 PM. The celebration continues on Friday\, June 20 at Cardin
 al Park located at 657 S Walnut St\, Pinebluff\, NC 28373 from 2 PM to 9 P
