DTSTAMP:20260702T041151Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53136312962574
DTSTART:20260619T200000Z
DTEND:20260620T030000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join The Plant for the Eyes Wide Open Juneteenth Festival on Fr
 i\, Jun 19\, 4pm-11pm. June 19th\, 1865\, is remembered around America as 
 the day the African American people were liberated from slavery. Years of 
 traditions\, culture\, and memories have been passed down since\, remindin
 g future generations of the hardships and struggles endured to get here to
 day. Eyes Wide Open is taking a spin on this cultural day\, providing a sp
 ace to share Black history and celebrate Black culture. The festival will 
 feature all-African American musical performances from the Raleigh area\, 
 as well as Black businesses at the forefront to support. Other activities 
 include a cards table\, double dutch\, face painting\, cornhole\, mega jen
 ga\, a photobooth\, and a vendor market. The schedule of performances is b
 elow:\n\n4pm-5:30pm DJ set.6pm EWO.6:15pm Antonenow.6:40pm Blatti.7:05pm X
 ae Recorded.7:30pm Overpade.8pm Intermission.8:30pm Dearxay.8:50pm Star Ki
 d.9:10pm Aleo.9:25pm Cocoa.10pm Njoki.The theme for this event is Black Da
 ndy. Doors open at 4pm. Admission is $17.50 online and $15 at the door. Mo
 st events are rain or shine\; if they have to be canceled\, they will do s
 o as far in advance as possible. Free parking is available onsite. Leashed
 \, well-behaved pets are allowed outside\; pet policies may vary by indivi
 dual business. The Plant is accessible to guests and will do its best to a
 ccommodate any additional requests. Please contact music@theplantnc.com wi
 th any accommodation requests or accessibility concerns. See all events at
  The Plant. Part of the Chatham County Craft Beverages & Country Inns Trai
 l.
GEO:35.709797;-79.156192
LOCATION:Plant
SUMMARY:Eyes Wide Open Juneteenth Festival
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/eyes-wide-open-juneteenth-fe
 stival
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Festivals & Fairs
END:VEVENT
