DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Juneteenth\, the Battleship North Carolina wi
 ll be illuminated in red\, white\, and blue\, honoring the end of slavery 
 in the United States and celebrating African American freedom\, resilience
 \, and culture.\n\nBeginning at sunset (around 8:30 pm)\, the Battleship
 ’s striking display will cast a glow across the Wilmington skyline—inv
 iting residents and visitors to pause\, reflect\, and gather in recognitio
 n of this important date in American history. The illumination will be vis
 ible from downtown Wilmington’s Riverwalk\, nearby parks\, and across th
 e Cape Fear River.\n\nAs North Carolina’s official World War II memorial
 \, the Battleship serves as a place for remembrance\, education\, and conn
 ection. This special illumination offers an opportunity for the community 
 to come together in reflection—acknowledging the past while looking ahea
 d with purpose and understanding.
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina
SUMMARY:Battleship NORTH CAROLINA Uplighting in Honor of Juneteenth
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battleship-north-carolina-up
 lighting-in-honor-of-juneteenth
END:VEVENT
