DESCRIPTION:Tour the Greensboro History Museum’s galleries and meet costu
 med interpreters portraying Guilford County’s Revolutionary residents\, 
 public figures\, and political activists. Visitors will meet Black Patriot
  Ishmael Titus\, Suffragist Laura Weil Cone\, Trailblazing Councilman Lonn
 ie Revels\, and more. Guided tours leave every 10-15 minutes from the muse
 um lobby.\n\nLifted Voices is a series of living history programs that bri
 ng to life people and stories from Greensboro’s past. This is a free\, f
 amily-friendly program. Join us for history in first person.
