UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53162383775691
DTSTART:20260622T220000Z
DTEND:20260622T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Outdoor NC Guide & Haw River native Ben Clarke and his tru
 sty dog Rocco for a lovely 2 mile round-trip loop hike along the east bank
  of the Haw between Highway 64 and the start of Jordan Lake. This free eve
 nt is part of the Take a Walk on the Wild Side hiking series offered by Fr
 iends of Lower Haw River. We'll cross several creeks\, pass some of the ri
 ver's most famous rapids\, and marvel at unique sights like the cactus bou
 lder and cedar rock! Please wear sturdy shoes for walking on uneven ground
  and bring adequate water. Friendly dogs are welcome on leash! No pre-regi
 stration required but contact us at lowerhawevents@gmail.com to let us kno
 w you are coming. Parking is limited – please carpool.\n\nLocation: GPS 
 35.7322\, -79.1046\n\nDirections:  From Pittsboro\, take US 64 east headed
  towards Apex. Slow down on the bridge crossing the Haw River. Immediately
  after crossing the river\, there is a small gravel parking area on the ri
 ght. Parking is limited.  For your safety\, do not park along the highway.
 \n\nFrom Apex\, take US 64 west headed towards Pittsboro.  After crossing 
 over the Haw River\, make a U-turn at the first left and head east on US 6
 4 back over the Haw River. Slow down on the bridge crossing the Haw River.
  Immediately after crossing the river\, there is a small gravel parking ar
 ea on the right. Parking is limited. For your safety\, do not park along t
 he highway.
LOCATION:GPS 35.7322\, -79.1046
SUMMARY:Take a Walk on the Wild Side: Haw River Lowlands Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/take-a-walk-on-the-wild-side
 -haw-river-lowlands-hike
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
END:VEVENT
