DESCRIPTION:In commemoration of America's 250th\, Atkins Library at UNC Cha
 rlotte presents the exhibit "Charlotte\, A Hornet’s Nest of Rebellion: A
 n Enduring Legacy from the Revolutionary War to Today." Using archives and
  rare books\, the exhibit tells the story of how Charlotte earned this rep
 utation\, tracing the history from British General Charles Cornwallis’s 
 1780 retreat from our region to sports mascots and modern-day social activ
 ism. Please check the Atkins Library website for open hours.
