DESCRIPTION:Although much has been written about George Washington\, one as
 pect of his life is typically underrepresented – His ability to adapt to
  the challenges in the early stages of the American Revolution.  Taking on
  the most powerful military force in the world forced Washington to freque
 ntly break with conventional thinking in his personal life and leadership.
   We will explore how George Washington and his compatriots successfully e
 ngaged the British in unexpected ways to form a nation.
GEO:35.690575;-82.569099
LOCATION:Dry Ridge Historical Museum
SUMMARY:George Washington\, his Compatriots\, and the Nascent American Revo
 lution
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/george-washington-his-compat
 riots-and-the-nascent-american-revolution
