DESCRIPTION:As America celebrates its 250th Birthday\, Charlotte-Mecklenbur
 g Animal Care & Control invites the community to participate in 250 Acts o
 f Freedom for Shelter Pets\, a one-day challenge focused on helping shelte
 r pets and pet owners throughout Mecklenburg County.\n\nThe goal is simple
 : complete 250 acts that benefit animals and the people who care for them.
  Community members can participate through pet adoption\, fostering\, volu
 nteer sign-ups\, volunteer service\, daycations\, staycations\, donations\
 , pet microchipping\, and other acts that support animal welfare.\n\nAs pa
 rt of the event\, Charlotte-Mecklenburg Animal Care & Control will also ho
 st a Free Microchip Clinic for the first 100 pets from 9:00 a.m. to 12:00 
 p.m.\, provided by Cherry Park Animal Hospital. The days surrounding Indep
 endence Day are among the busiest times of the year for lost pets\, and mi
 crochipping is one of the most effective ways to help reunite lost pets wi
 th their families.\n\nWhether you choose to adopt\, foster\, volunteer\, d
 onate\, take a shelter dog on a daycation\, or microchip your pet\, every 
 act helps shelter pets experience a little more freedom.\n\nJoin us as we 
 celebrate 250 years of American independence through 250 Acts of Freedom f
 or Shelter Pets.
GEO:35.190897;-80.948371
LOCATION:Charlotte-Mecklenburg Animal Care & Control
SUMMARY:250 Acts of Freedom for Shelter Pets
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/250-acts-of-freedom-for-shel
 ter-pets-4948
