DESCRIPTION:You are invited to attend a special and commemorative event at 
 the Davie County Public Library. Our Founding Fathers signed the Declarati
 on of Independence on August 2\, 1776. Nevertheless\, they officially adop
 ted it on July 4 of that same year. \n\nOn Thursday\, July 2\, from 2-6 pm
 \, the library's Martin-Wall History Room will allow the public to sign an
 d take home their own copy of the infamous document. Those in attendance w
 ill also be allowed to hear others read it aloud. There will be artifacts 
 on display\, including original land grants and the Squire Boone long rifl
 e. You will even be given the chance to use an ink quill pen\, the same it
 em used to write and sign the infamous document! \n\nPlease use this oppor
 tunity to make memories this Independence Day\, aside from the barbecues a
 nd fireworks! Sponsored by the Davie County Historical and Genealogical So
 ciety.
GEO:35.897815;-80.5597
LOCATION:Davie County Library\, Martin-Wall History Room
