DESCRIPTION:Join park staff for a guided Flytrap Hike and discover the incr
 edible diversity of life found at Carolina Beach State Park. This easy\, f
 amily-friendly program follows a flat\, 0.5-mile loop trail\, making it pe
 rfect for participants of all ages. Along the way\, we’ll explore severa
 l distinct ecosystems and learn about the unique plants and animals that c
 all the park home\, including the Venus flytrap. Participants will learn m
 ore about carnivorous plants\, including how and why they eat insects. Be 
 sure to wear sturdy walking shoes and sun protection to stay comfortable o
 n the trail. Water\, sunscreen\, and bug spray are also recommended. Meet 
 in the Flytrap Trail parking area.
GEO:34.045859;-77.905159
LOCATION:Carolina Beach State Park\, Flytrap Trail
SUMMARY:Flytrap Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/flytrap-hike-4940
