DESCRIPTION:This Independence Day\, celebrate America's 250 with a guided h
 ike that brings local history to life through the lens of our living landm
 arks: witness trees. Participants will learn how to identify and age sever
 al species of trees along the Piedmont Loop Trail\, trees which served as 
 silent observers to events of the past and to the history being made each 
 day.\n\nTrail distance is 1.4 miles\, "easy" but traveling over some short
 \, steeper inclines. Bring what you need to be comfortable\, dress for the
  weather\, and please wear close-toed walking shoes (for stepping short di
 stances off trail to measure trees). Recommended for adults and youth ages
  five and older. Registration suggested but not required.
