BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041153Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52930065311734
DTSTART:20260704T130000Z
DTEND:20260704T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Tryon Palcae as we celebrate our county’s semiquincenten
 nial–the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independ
 ence!\n\nThe day will begin with a performance by the Tryon Palace Fife an
 d Drum Corps and an Interpretive Reading of the Declaration of Independenc
 e by the front gates of Tryon Palace. After the reading\, the Grounds and 
 Gardens will be open to the public until noon. Immediately following the r
 eading\, the Fife and Drum Corps will march off the Palace Grounds to take
  their place at the head of the New Bern Independence Day Parade and lead 
 the parade it its final destination. For parade route information\, please
  see City of New Bern resources.\n\nWe are also offering our Caswell’s C
 apital tour on Glorious Fourth. The 3:30 P.M. tour will be Caswell’s Cap
 ital\, with the remainder of the tours being our standard Palace tour.\n\n
 Be sure to stop by the North Carolina History Center to see our A250 NC ex
 hibit\, Freedom and Identity: Symbols of a New Nation. This exhibit contai
 ns items from the Tryon Palace Collection that pertain to the American Rev
 olution and the earliest days of our nation–including items that are new
  to our collections and will be displayed for the first time at Tryon Pala
 ce.\n\nPhiladelphia held the first annual commemoration of independence on
  July 4\, 1777\, while Congress was still occupied with the ongoing war. N
 ew Bern first celebrated Independence Day in 1778.\n\nAdmittance to the Ga
 rdens is FREE until 12 Noon. Tryon Palace tours are available with purchas
 e of One Day Pass. Caswell’s Capital tour requires a separate ticket.
GEO:35.104831;-77.043044
LOCATION:Tryon Palace Historic Sites and Gardens
SUMMARY:Tryon Palace Glorious 4th: An A250 NC Event
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/tryon-palace-glorious-4th-an
 -a250-nc-event
