BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041153Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51499113410036
DTSTART:20260704T140000Z
DTEND:20260704T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Fourth of July at Old Salem!\n\nDid you know the 
 first official Fourth of July Celebration in North Carolina was held in Ol
 d Salem? In 1783\, Governor Alexander Martin proclaimed July 4th a day of 
 thanksgiving and peace\, and Salem residents gathered for food\, fellowshi
 p\, and festivities. This year\, we invite you to be part of that traditio
 n.\n\nJoin us for a full day of music\, history\, and hands-on experiences
  as we welcome visitors of all ages to commemorate Independence Day at the
  site of North Carolina’s very first July 4th celebration.\n\nExplore Ol
 d Salem Museums & Gardens—a historic site sharing the stories of Moravia
 n\, Black\, and Indigenous peoples in the American South. Our museums\, hi
 storic town\, and gardens offer an immersive and memorable historical expe
 rience for all visitors.\n\nEvent Highlights\n\nRevolutionary War–Era Mu
 sic\nHear authentic period music and learn how troops used sound as a comm
 unication tool during the war. Enjoy worship pieces composed by Moravian m
 usicians—just as Salem residents did in their weekly services.\n\nHistor
 ic Demonstrations\n• Fire Bucket Brigade – Discover how early firefigh
 ters managed emergencies before hand-pumped engines.\n• Historic Firearm
 s – Watch demonstrations of the types of firearms crafted and used in Sa
 lem.\n• Frozen Treat Making – Visit the Vogler House to see how early 
 Salem residents created one of America’s favorite sweet treats.\n\nDecla
 ration of Independence Readings\nJoin us throughout the day for readings o
 f the Declaration of Independence in honor of the 250th anniversary of its
  signing.\n\nGuided Tours\nMeet our costumed interpreters and explore the 
 Historic Town of Salem on a guided tour.\n\nAll activities are included wi
 th standard ticket admission. Reserve your spot today and celebrate the Fo
 urth of July in historic style!
GEO:36.083505;-80.24289
LOCATION:Old Salem Museums & Gardens\, Old Salem Visitor Center and the His
 toric District
SUMMARY:Independence Day Celebration at Old Salem
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/independence-day-celebration
 -at-old-salem
