DESCRIPTION:Join us for our homegrown July 4th celebration the HEARTS way\,
  sharing local history\, nature\, the arts\, and incredible live music! \n
 \nThe connection to Lincoln County’s iron-rich history is the highlight 
 at HEARTS 250 on July 4th! If you’re looking for a unique experience on 
 the 250th anniversary of the Declaration of Independence\, look no further
 \, you've found it!\n\nFrom 2:00-5:00 at Cedar Grove and the Hugh Torance 
 House and Store\, join us for a very special living history day featuring 
 blacksmith demonstrations\, metal forging in our region\, historic artifac
 ts\, and more! We’ll also have hot dogs (veggie and not)\, beverages\, a
 nd the historic store is stocked with artisanal goodies to check out\, too
 !  Our live music for the day is a stellar trio! Presenting Heidi Sidelink
 er\, Billy Jones\, and the legendary Jim Brock! Yes\, THE Jim Brock!
