DESCRIPTION:Join Salem Band for an All-American band concert in the town Sq
 uare\, our Annual Stars & Stripes performance honoring veterans in our com
 munity with marches\, big bands\, sing-alongs\, Armed Forces Salute\, and 
 of course\, Star & Stripes Forever! Hear two World Premieres of original c
 ompositions celebrating our nation’s 250th Anniversary and the original 
 Independence Day celebration in Salem Square: Healthy\, Wealthy\, and Wise
  by Steven Sherrill\; and American Hussite by David Mailman. The program i
 ncludes Tchaikovsky’s 1812 Overture\, Places USA\, and Cosmopolitan Amer
 ica. Don’t miss the sibling vocal duo featuring our own SB vocalist Mign
 on Dobbins and brother David Dobbins\, baritone – singing\, song-leading
 \, and narrating.  Arrive at 6:45 pm to enjoy pre-concert jazz by The Luke
  Childress Quartet. This event is generously supported by a grant from The
  Winston-Salem Foundation.\n\nFREE in Salem Square\, Old Salem\, Winston-S
 alem. Bring a lawn chair or blanket and a picnic. Rain-date = Sunday\, Jul
 y 05.\n\nEstablished in 1771\, Salem Band is the oldest\, continuous mixed
  wind ensemble in the nation. Eileen Young\, Music Director. \n\nwww.salem
 band.org \n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/SalemBandFan/
