DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the 250th anniversary of the first public reading of 
 the Declaration of Independence on 8 July 1776 by attending a 2026 public 
 reading of the Declaration of Independence.\n\n\nJoin members of Franklin 
 County's Del Webb at Traditions Veteran's Club for the 250th anniversary o
 f the reading of the Declaration of Independence on the steps of the State
  House in Philadelphia (now Independence Hall) July 8\, 1776. The Declarat
 ion will be read by guest speakers from the Franklin County community and 
 local government at exactly noon.  Refreshments will be served from 11:30a
 m - 2:30pm.  Come enjoy lunch\, support local veterans and listen to the w
 ords of the Declaration of Independence from the lens of modern day Americ
 a.  All members of community are encouraged to join the festivities.  Ther
 e is no cost to attend. The Del Webb at Traditions Veteran's Club will be 
 collecting donations at this event to support local veteran organizations.
 \n\n\nThis is a community event that is endorsed by the Franklin County Am
 erica 250 committee.
GEO:36.005359;-78.490283
LOCATION:Bud's Tavern
