X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041154Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52992358883442
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260711
DESCRIPTION:This self-paced course runs from Tuesday\, June 16 to Tuesday\,
  August 11. Participants can start any time between June 16 and August 4.\
 n\nHow can art be used to develop student growth in literacy skills? This 
 self-paced online course explores methods for integrating art and literacy
  strategies to support North Carolina’s Literacy Instruction Standards a
 cross classrooms. Participants gain an understanding of how literacy is de
 fined through a variety of lenses and apply their learning by developing a
  lesson plan. Strategies that incorporate NCMA works of art are used to pr
 actice and apply activities to build interpretive and expressive modes of 
 literacy focused on a variety of reading materials\, comprehension\, vocab
 ulary building\, and writing. This course is designed for teachers of all 
 disciplines and audiences. A certificate of participation for 20 hours wil
 l be provided for literacy\, general\, or content area credits (2 CEU\, wi
 th prior approval from the local school system).
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:NCMA Online Course for Educators: Art and Literacy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncma-online-course-for-educa
 tors-art-and-literacy
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041154Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53302861014288
DTSTART:20260711T070000Z
DTEND:20260711T080000Z
DESCRIPTION:Opera Lite: American Odyssey \n\nA song recital celebrating 250
  years of the American experience \n\nPerformed at the Davidson County His
 torical Museum\, sponsored by The Edward C. Smith Civic Center. \n\nPresen
 ted as a live radio broadcast\, American Odyssey takes audiences on a jour
 ney through 250 years of American song\, from the parlor and the revival t
 o the protest march and the Broadway stage. Hosted at the historic Davidso
 n County Courthouse in Lexington\, NC\, this recital traces the story of A
 merica through its music\, connecting major moments in American history an
 d legal tradition to the songs that defined them. Featuring works drawn fr
 om the many communities that make up the American story\, performed by Rev
 erend Kenneth Alexander Pettigrew\, Logan Webber and Arianna Bohning\, thi
 s is a chance to reflect on\, appreciate and celebrate the full American e
 xperience. \n\nA part of The Opera Lite series through Piedmont Opera. \n\
 nWhat is Opera LITE?\n\nWhether you're opera-curious or a lifelong fan\, O
 pera LITE is designed to make opera approachable\, engaging\, and fun. Thi
 s casual concert series features classically trained rising artists in an 
 informal setting that combines beautiful singing with storytelling\, histo
 rical context\, artist conversations\, and audience Q&A. Rather than a tra
 ditional staged opera\, Opera LITE offers themed performances that invite 
 audiences to experience extraordinary vocal artistry without the formality
  often associated with opera.\n\n"I couldn't be more excited to welcome Pi
 edmont Opera for this special performance\," said Caitlin Williams-Cole\, 
 curator of the Davidson County Historical Museum. "I attended my first Ope
 ra LITE concert earlier this year and was blown away. The performers are t
 ruly world-class. I was impressed by how interactive the experience was. T
 hey entertained\, educated\, and connected with the audience from beginnin
 g to end. Even as someone who knew very little about opera\, I left a fan\
 , and I think you will too."\n\nTickets: $15\nLimited seating. Advance pur
 chase recommended.\nSaturday\, July 11\, 2026 • 3:00 p.m.\nDavidson Coun
 ty Historical Museum\n2 South Main Street\nLexington\, NC 27292
GEO:35.82403;-80.253694
LOCATION:Davidson County Historical Museum\, Historic Courtroom
SUMMARY:American Odyssey: A Song Recital Celebrating 250 Years of the Ameri
 can Experience
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/american-odyssey-a-song-reci
 tal-celebrating-250-years-of-the-american-experience
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Concerts (Music)
CATEGORIES:Theater & Musicals
END:VEVENT
