DESCRIPTION:⚓☀️ Sailors in the Summer: Naval Living History ☀️⚓
 \n📍 CSS Neuse Civil War Museum\n\nExperience history firsthand at the C
 SS Neuse Civil War Museum during our third annual Sailors in the Summer: N
 aval Living History event! Step into the world of Civil War sailors on Sat
 urday\, July 11\, 2026\, from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\, and discover what 
 life was like on—and under—the water during the war.\n\n\n👕🎖️ 
 Throughout the day\, naval living history reenactors\, museum staff\, and 
 volunteers will bring history to life by sharing stories about sailors’ 
 daily experiences—from the food they ate and games they played to the to
 ols\, weapons\, and skills they used. \n\n🛠️⚓ Hands-on fun for all 
 ages!\n\nExplore engaging\, naval-themed activities and exhibits\, includi
 ng:\nRope-making demonstrations 🪢🪢\n\nLearn about ironclad ships\, b
 lockade running\, and naval stores such as tar\, pitch\, and turpentine—
 essential materials that kept ships afloat. ⚓🛢️\n\nExplore a torped
 o display and learn how these early naval weapons were used during the Civ
 il War 💣🌊\n\nExamine fascinating artifacts from the museum’s colle
 ction 🔍\n\nEnjoy a family-friendly scavenger hunt 👨‍👩‍👧‍
 👦\n\nStaff members from the Museum of the Albemarle will be here to all
 ow visitors to explore an archaeology outreach kit focused on underwater a
 rchaeology\, shipwrecks\, and how archaeologists study and protect submerg
 ed cultural resources 🌊⚓\n\n🚢✨ Special Guest \nBruce\, a board m
 ember from The Friends of the Hunley\, will join us to discuss the history
 \, construction\, and conservation of the legendary H.L. Hunley submarine.
  \n\n🎟️ Admission Rates\n$5+tax – Adults\n$4+tax – Senior Citizen
 s & Veterans\n$3+tax– Students\nFree – Children ages 3 and under\n\nBl
 ue Star Museums Program \n\nThe CSS Neuse Museum is proud to participate i
 n Blue Star Museums. All active-duty military personnel with a valid ID an
 d their families (up to five members) receive free admission from Saturday
 \, May 16\, 2026\, through Labor Day\, Monday\, September 7\, 2026\n\n📧
  Questions?\nEmail Rachel at rachel.kennedy@dncr.nc.gov or call 252-526-96
 00\, ext. 221 or 222.\n\n🌊⚓🪢 Bring the whole crew and dive into an
  unforgettable day of naval history\, underwater archaeology\, and summer 
 fun—we can’t wait to welcome you!
GEO:35.260403;-77.581573
LOCATION:CSS Neuse Civil War Museum
SUMMARY:Sailors in the Summer: Naval Living History 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/sailors-in-the-summer-naval-
 living-history
