DESCRIPTION:**UPDATE** This workshop has been moved to a virtual meeting. P
 lease register using the form below\, and you will receive a meeting link 
 closer to the day of the session.\n\n \n\nThomas Day State Historic Site i
 nvites K-12 educators to join us for a two-hour   professional development
  workshop that explores the roles of local history and primary sources in 
 shaping meaningful instruction\, with a focused look at Caswell County's s
 chool desegregation story.\n\nThrough a blend of hands-on research and dis
 cussion\, participants will learn how to discover\, analyze\, and teach wi
 th local primary sources to help students connect national history to thei
 r own communities. This session is completely free of charge\, and catered
  lunch is provided at no additional cost. Participants may receive .45 CEU
  credits. \n\nWhile the workshop is designed for K-12 classroom teachers\,
  educators (current or former) of any kind are encouraged to register. \n\
 nPlease complete the form to register: https://forms.gle/eLbAryWhQym3vpig7
