UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138241938406
DTSTART:20260804T140000Z
DTEND:20260804T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041155Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083027756
DTSTART:20260804T140000Z
DTEND:20260804T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for sur
 vival\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fight
 s back in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the 
 world with unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with tr
 ippy toads\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover h
 ow these defenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage an
 d mimicry\, specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink
  bombs\, caboose cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, st
 and their ground or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live ani
 mal encounters\, larger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and 
 interactive programs.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of al
 l ages. Offered in English & Spanish.
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
