BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041155Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53031774659142
DTSTART:20260810T230000Z
DTEND:20260811T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:America 250 Speaker Series\nHonoring the Stories. Understanding
  Our History.\n\nJoin the AAHGS North Carolina Triangle Chapter for our Am
 erica 250 Speaker Series\, a four-part virtual educational program highlig
 hting the lives\, service\, contributions\, and legacies of African Americ
 ans and other People of Color whose stories have often been overlooked in 
 traditional historical narratives.\n\nAs our nation commemorates the 250th
  anniversary of the United States\, this series brings together respected 
 genealogists\, historians\, researchers\, and educators to explore Revolut
 ionary War history\, family history\, local history\, and lineage research
  through a broader and more inclusive lens.\n\nFeatured Speakers\n• Tany
 a Foreman – June 8\, 2026\n• Saundra Cropps – July 13\, 2026\n• Ri
 c Murphy – August 10\, 2026\n• Charlotte Chatfield – September 14\, 
 2026\n\nEvent Details\n📅 Second Monday of each month (June–September 
 2026)\n🕖 7:00 PM Eastern Time\n💻 Live via Zoom\n💲 FREE to Attend\
 n🌎 Open to the Public\n\nRegistration Required\n\nAlthough this series 
 is free\, registration is required to receive the Zoom access information.
  The good news is that you only need to register once. When you register f
 or any session\, you will automatically be registered for all four present
 ations and will receive the Zoom links needed to participate throughout th
 e series.\n\nWhether you are a genealogist\, historian\, educator\, studen
 t\, lineage society member\, or simply someone who enjoys learning about A
 merica's diverse history\, this series offers a unique opportunity to disc
 over stories that deserve to be remembered and shared.\n\nRegister today a
 nd join us as we celebrate America 250 by honoring the stories and underst
 anding our history.\n\nREGISTER TODAY FREE EVENT!!!
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AAHGS NC Triangle Chapter America 250 Speaker Series
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/aahgs-nc-triangle-chapter-am
 erica-250-speaker-series
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041155Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52737863762694
DTSTART:20260810T230000Z
DTEND:20260811T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Amplifying diverse Appalachian voices\n\nMusic and dance have b
 een a vital part of the Folk School since its founding in 1925. As we cele
 brate our 100th year\, Centennial Sounds honors this legacy by spotlight
 ing the cultural richness of Appalachian music and the many voices that sh
 ape it. This special performance series will feature five headliners whose
  work expands and redefines the story of Appalachian music. Through these 
 concerts\, we aim to create new opportunities for our community in Western
  North Carolina to experience the full spectrum of Appalachian sound.\n\nT
 he Folk School is supported by the North Carolina Arts Council\, a divisio
 n of the Department of Natural and Cultural Resources.
GEO:35.03748;-83.964153
LOCATION:Folk School Festival Barn
SUMMARY:Centennial Sounds
