BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260702T041156Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52683590241755
DTSTART:20260823T140000Z
DTEND:20260823T153000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Clarion Call of Liberty and Independence\, April 26\, 2026\
 n\nContinuing Wilmington Water Tours’ commemoration of the United State
 ’s 250th anniversary\, join Dr. Chris E. Fonvielle Jr.\, Professor Emeri
 tus in the Dept. of History at UNCW continues discussing the decline of th
 e British Empire after the French and Indian War in 1763 and the rise of a
  great nation by 1887.  This cruise covers an in-depth discussion about Gr
 eat Britain’s grand plan for a military campaign against the Southern co
 lonies by way of the Cape Fear River in 1776\; and the decisive Battle of 
 Moore’s Creek Bridge based on Dr. Fonvielle’s latest research and fort
 hcoming book.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong history buff or just curious 
 about the forces that shaped this region\, this is a one-of-a-kind opportu
 nity to learn while enjoying a relaxing\, scenic cruise. Topics rotate mon
 thly\, so every trip offers a new perspective on Wilmington’s place in A
 merican history.  The next two cruises will be April 26\, and May 24.\n\nO
 ur boat\, The Wilmington\, has comfortable seating for up to 49 passengers
 \, refreshments for all ages at the bar and a restroom on board. This is a
  90 minute cruise $45 adults\, $25 children. Boarding is 15 minutes prior 
 to departure.
GEO:34.232504;-77.949383
LOCATION:Wilmington Water Tours LLC\, On the Riverwalk
SUMMARY:History Comes Alive with Historian Dr. Chris Fonvielle
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-comes-alive-with-his
 torian-dr-chris-fonvielle-4988
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
